description:
Suggests a link between two of the reader's saved quotes in ReadingRate, with a line on why they belong together. The suggestion waits in the app until the reader accepts or dismisses it; it is not a link until they accept.

Use when you notice two of the reader's quotes, usually from different books, that speak to each other in a way the reader may not have seen, and the reader has not asked you to link them. Say in the conversation which two you suggested and why. Check list_quote_links first so you do not suggest a link they already have.

Example: {"quote_id": "<quote id>", "linked_quote_id": "<quote id>", "note": "Both describe living only in the present."}
